{"case": "self", "turn": 1, "generated": {"status": "complete", "move": "T05"}, "reply": "The main choice is between Original Medicare and Medicare Advantage. Original Medicare is Parts A and B from the federal program; you can add a separate drug plan and may be able to add Medigap. Medicare Advantage is a private plan that provides Parts A and B, and many plans include drug coverage.", "question": "What health insurance do you have now?", "visual": "routes", "seconds": 0.087, "synthetic_replay": true}
{"case": "self", "turn": 2, "generated": {"status": "complete", "move": "RC09"}, "reply": "That helps because current-job coverage can affect when it makes sense to start Medicare, especially Part B. I can’t tell from that alone whether you’d want to enroll right away or keep employer coverage for a while.", "question": "Whose job is this health insurance through?", "visual": "none", "seconds": 0.038, "synthetic_replay": true}
{"case": "self", "turn": 3, "generated": {"status": "complete", "move": "RC09"}, "reply": "Yes. There are two main paths: Original Medicare and Medicare Advantage. Original Medicare is Part A and Part B through the federal program; you can usually add a separate drug plan, and Medigap may help with out-of-pocket costs. Medicare Advantage is a private plan approved by Medicare that provides Parts A and B, and many plans include drug coverage. With either path, you still pay the Part B premium.", "question": "Whose job is this health insurance through?", "visual": "routes", "seconds": 7.351}
{"case": "caregiver", "turn": 1, "generated": {"status": "complete", "move": "RC01"}, "reply": "Your mother will usually start by choosing between two Medicare paths: Original Medicare, which is Part A and Part B through the federal program, or a Medicare Advantage plan, which is a private plan that provides Part A and Part B. With Original Medicare, drug coverage is separate and Medigap may help with out-of-pocket costs; with Medicare Advantage, drug coverage is often included, and doctors, medicines, and total costs are important to check before choosing.", "question": "Who is this for?", "visual": "none", "seconds": 9.496}
{"case": "caregiver", "turn": 2, "generated": {"status": "complete", "move": "RC01"}, "reply": "Part B is the medical insurance part of Medicare. It covers doctor visits, outpatient care, tests, medical equipment, and many preventive services like certain screenings. Together, Part A and Part B make up Original Medicare.", "question": "Who is this for?", "visual": "none", "seconds": 5.36}
